45585] [17592186125654 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "7440cca3-653a-5d59-a5d4-2b047f4c7357" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186125654 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186125894 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186125889 #edb/ref 1064 "A table showing the most common cylinders whose base curve is centered at the origin in the $xy$-plane is given below.\n\n| Surface | Equation | Image |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Elliptic Cylinder | $\\dfrac{x^2}{a^2}+\\dfrac{y^2}{b^2} = 1$ | ![](images/2b/2b8788f027b93593a025542face33546425b057d1eb3b8e18da26e7774f6ed20.png) |\n| Parabolic Cylinder | $x^2=4py$<br><br>$y^2=4px$ | ![](images/d3/d3f31aae01222e6a63e5de185c5b9f5a8af5aed8a750c6bc230e20e9fd93871a.png) |\n| Hyperbolic Cylinder | $\\dfrac{x^2}{a^2}-\\dfrac{y^2}{b^2}=1$<br><br>$\\dfrac{y^2}{b^2}-\\dfrac{x^2}{a^2}=1$ | ![](images/15/159bb67600e079d9943ba6f79fcc6e580e3718f822dce50620c2bb6d2d9b76c8.png) |\n\nSimilar to quadric surfaces:\n\n- We can generate cylinders with alternative orientation axes by describing a base curve in the $xz$-or $yz$-planes.\n\nFor example, the equation of an elliptic cylinder with its axis of symmetry along the $y$-axis is given by $$\\dfrac{x^2}{a^2} + \\dfrac{z^2}{c^2} = 1.$$\n- We can shift the center/vertex of the base curve in the usual way." #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186125889 #edb/ref 1065 7843 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186125889 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "41c3acb2-b2af-59b4-a6bb-3883e59406f4" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186125889 #edb/ref 1067 "A Table of Common Cylinders" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186125894 #edb/ref 1064 "The most common quadric surfaces are those centered at the origin. We describe these common surfaces in the table below.\n\n| Surface | Equation | Image |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Ellipsoid | $\\dfrac{x^2}{a^2}+\\dfrac{y^2}{b^2}+\\dfrac{z^2}{c^2} = 1$ | ![](images/09/09dc100248a28a5518bcd8428368edefc7c3ee8d5ef0e50515cb7552ee54a376.png) |\n| Elliptic Paraboloid | $z = \\dfrac{x^2}{a^2}+\\dfrac{y^2}{b^2}$ | ![](images/76/76e4ad8cb1e83eadae4dce865e100c9a716f9830e7f12adb367b2a9b74d1a651.png) |\n| Hyperbolic Paraboloid | $z = \\dfrac{x^2}{a^2}-\\dfrac{y^2}{b^2}$ | ![](images/cb/cbc04d7f98e1bb7ce0d62eda71102a6abad708dfcedd7aabee8fff23281471dd.png) |\n| Hyperboloid of One Sheet | $\\dfrac{x^2}{a^2}+\\dfrac{y^2}{b^2}-\\dfrac{z^2}{c^2}=1$ | ![](images/df/df6ef914bc78e121d75baf9f5147784d0e6e434d76800eff60dcb3c3d764477c.png) |\n| Hyperboloid of Two Sheets | $\\dfrac{x^2}{a^2}+\\dfrac{y^2}{b^2}-\\dfrac{z^2}{c^2}=-1$ | ![](images/08/0870b95c5ce1133d6645e3063174157e36c4354df370c05e48218111ea714838.png) |\n| Elliptic Cone | $\\dfrac{z^2}{c^2}=\\dfrac{x^2}{a^2}+\\dfrac{y^2}{b^2}$ | ![](images/0f/0f492bf07e573ec7858977e48fa4bf81635e61520b5caa9edef14bd259184347.png) |\n\nAlso, recall the following from previous lessons:\n\n- We can generate paraboloids, hyperboloids, and cones with alternative orientation axes by permuting the variables in the corresponding equation.\n\nFor example, the equation of an elliptic cone with its vertex at $O$ and axis of symmetry along the $y$-axis is given by $$\\dfrac{y^2}{b^2} = \\dfrac{x^2}{a^2} + \\dfrac{z^2}{c^2}.$$\n- We can shift the center/vertex/saddle point of a quadric surface to $(x_0,y_0,z_0)$ using the usual coordinate transformation: $$(x,y,z) \\longrightarrow (x-x_0,y-y_0,z-z_0)$$\n\nFinally, there is a simple way to distinguish between hyperboloids with one and two sheets by simply looking at the equations:\n\n- *one* minus sign indicates hyperboloids of *one* sheet: $$\\dfrac{x^2}{a^2}+\\dfrac{y^2}{b^2} \\bbox[3pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{red}-} \\dfrac{z^2}{c^2}=1$$\n- *two* minus signs indicate hyperboloids of *two* sheets: $$\\dfrac{x^2}{a^2}+\\dfrac{y^2}{b^2} \\bbox[3pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{red}-} \\dfrac{z^2}{c^2}= \\bbox[3pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{red}-}1$$" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186125894 #edb/ref 1065 7860 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186125894 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "e806c3d0-0e3e-584e-93eb-1406ac607ad3" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186125894 #edb/ref 1067 "Introduction" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186281850 #edb/ref 1081 "A hyperbolic paraboloid centered at $(-1,2,3)$" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186281850 #edb/ref 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186281850 #edb/ref 1084 #uuid "10cde161-28f6-55e5-986b-ad9855da614a" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186281869 #edb/ref 1081 "A hyperbolic paraboloid centered at $(1,-2,3)$" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186281869 #edb/ref 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186281869 #edb/ref 1084 #uuid "122b7f1a-d06c-5752-b881-d3aaf0a1f656" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186282006 #edb/ref 1081 "A parabolic cylinder whose axis is the $x$-axis" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186282006 #edb/ref 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186282006 #edb/ref 1084 #uuid "232f26c9-79a9-5402-b0f7-63e58ec7851c" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186282319 #edb/ref 1081 "An ellipsoid centered at $(1,2,-3)$" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186282319 #edb/ref 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186282319 #edb/ref 1084 #uuid "49873a52-1e06-5d10-9048-c31a56b3f6fa" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186282767 #edb/ref 1081 "A couple of planes" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186282767 #edb/ref 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186282767 #edb/ref 1084 #uuid "7c568ec1-5072-5178-846a-7f2b606d9954" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186282958 #edb/ref 1081 "An elliptic cylinder whose axis is the $x$-axis" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186282958 #edb/ref 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186282958 #edb/ref 1084 #uuid "9283fa33-e3d9-51e6-a60b-d84331b8323d" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186283463 #edb/ref 1081 "A hyperbolic paraboloid centered at $(1,2,-3)$" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186283463 #edb/ref 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186283463 #edb/ref 1084 #uuid "ca420948-0b66-53de-bd82-72e7dc4965ff" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186283498 #edb/ref 1081 "An elliptic cylinder whose axis is the $y$-axis" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186283498 #edb/ref 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186283498 #edb/ref 1084 #uuid "ce57cf6e-a823-5536-bf65-94a57901af34" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186283586 #edb/ref 1081 "An elliptic paraboloid centered at $(1,2,-3)$" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186283586 #edb/ref 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186283586 #edb/ref 1084 #uuid "d9275452-1c1f-54aa-9f44-b0b79feef1b1" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186283778 #edb/ref 1081 "A parabolic cylinder whose axis is the $y$-axis" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186283778 #edb/ref 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186283778 #edb/ref 1084 #uuid "eefd41c3-ba1b-5b3d-8bc1-3c2122e2528a" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186283949 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186282006 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186283949 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186282767 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186283949 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186282958 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186283949 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186283498 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186283949 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186283778 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186283949 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186283949 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186283949 #edb/ref 1079 #edb/ref 17592186282006 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186283949 #edb/ref 1080 #uuid "05d7e5ed-5266-504a-b7eb-960c915d96ad" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186284388 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186281850 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186284388 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186281869 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186284388 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186282319 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186284388 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186283463 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186284388 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186283586 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186284388 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186284388 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186284388 #edb/ref 1079 #edb/ref 17592186283463 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186284388 #edb/ref 1080 #uuid "fd434c9b-d384-57dd-8332-85e7b5ec2000" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186284516 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186283949 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186284516 #edb/ref 1069 "q-164548" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186284516 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186284516 #edb/ref 1071 "Identify the following surface:\n\n$$\n{z}^{2}=-12y,\\,-\\infty <x<\\infty .\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186284516 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "fe349944-268d-5340-92ca-d28764061da5" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186284516 #edb/ref 1074 "Recall that the equation of a parabolic cylinder whose axis is the $z$-axis is given by\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}=4py.\n$$\n\nThus, a parabolic cylinder whose axis is the $x$**-axis** is given by\n\n$$\n{z}^{2}=4py.\n$$\n\nTherefore, our equation is a parabolic cylinder whose axis is the $x$-axis and $p=-3.$" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186284517 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186284388 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186284517 #edb/ref 1069 "q-164549" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186284517 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186284517 #edb/ref 1071 "Identify the surface ${y}^{2}-{z}^{2}-x-4y-6z-4=0.$" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186284517 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "1b66372b-0da7-5bff-8ad5-ecdf16f5fac5" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186284517 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we complete the square in the $y$ and $z$ terms:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{2}-{z}^{2}-x-4y-6z-4 & =0 \\\\ ({y}^{2}-4y)-({z}^{2}+6z)-x-4 & =0 \\\\ (y-2)^{2}-4-(z+3)^{2}+9-x-4 & =0 \\\\ (y-2)^{2}-(z+3)^{2}+1-x & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, by rearranging, we get the equation\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(y-2)^{2}-(z+3)^{2}+1-x & =0 \\\\ (y-2)^{2}-(z+3)^{2} & =x-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis is the equation of a hyperbolic paraboloid centered at $(1,2,-3).$" #edb/ref 17592186045585]}
